1e:["$","p","OutBrick is intentionally not a social feed. Still, a puzzle can become a shared object when someone explains the bottleneck, sends a screenshot of a clear, or asks a friend how they read the same shape. The board is a small place for interpretation.",{"children":"OutBrick is intentionally not a social feed. Still, a puzzle can become a shared object when someone explains the bottleneck, sends a screenshot of a clear, or asks a friend how they read the same shape. The board is a small place for interpretation."}]
1f:["$","p","The journal extends that space. We write about design choices so a player can see the thinking around the game, not just its surface. The goal is to make a solitary pause feel connected to a larger practice of noticing.",{"children":"The journal extends that space. We write about design choices so a player can see the thinking around the game, not just its surface. The goal is to make a solitary pause feel connected to a larger practice of noticing."}]
20:["$","p",null,{"className":"article-source-note","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Research trail"}],[["$","a","animal-crossing-routines-2021",{"href":"#reference-animal-crossing-routines-2021","aria-label":"Jump to source: Comerford (2021)","children":["[",1,"]"]}],["$","a","mit-social-mobile-2015",{"href":"#reference-mit-social-mobile-2015","aria-label":"Jump to source: Sra & Schmandt (2015)","children":["[",3,"]"]}]]]}]
21:["$","section","design-for-returning-together",{"id":"design-for-returning-together","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Design for returning together"}],[["$","p","The kindest shared spaces do not demand identical schedules. They leave a trace that can be picked up later, and they make room for different levels of participation. A person can visit for five minutes, decorate one corner, or simply see what changed.",{"children":"The kindest shared spaces do not demand identical schedules. They leave a trace that can be picked up later, and they make room for different levels of participation. A person can visit for five minutes, decorate one corner, or simply see what changed."}],["$","p","That is a useful standard for OutBrick’s wider ecosystem: every board should stand on its own, while the stories around the boards give players more ways to feel accompanied.",{"children":"That is a useful standard for OutBrick’s wider ecosystem: every board should stand on its own, while the stories around the boards give players more ways to feel accompanied."}]],null,null,["$","p",null,{"className":"article-source-note","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Research trail"}],[["$","a","animal-crossing-routines-2021",{"href":"#reference-animal-crossing-routines-2021","aria-label":"Jump to source: Comerford (2021)","children":["[",1,"]"]}],["$","a","gaming-fit-2025",{"href":"#reference-gaming-fit-2025","aria-label":"Jump to source: Ballou et al. (2025)","children":["[",4,"]"]}]]]}]]}]
